    "strict_watertight_gate_passed": true,
    "enclosed_voids_remaining": 0,
    "claims": "a study object derived from the twin with declared stock and fills; not a build file, no support, no machining drawing, and no dimension of the specimen"
   },
   "twin_surface_it_derives_from": {
    "record": "params/scorecard-v2-loft-s025.json",
    "checker": "score_twin.py (independent of producers); NVIDIA Warp mesh_query_point_no_sign on CPU",
    "share_of_the_area_on_acquired_scan": 0.81924,
    "limits": "distances to the acquired surface only; says nothing about unobserved geometry, physical calibration or function"
   }
  },
  "verdict": "admissible as a closed study body, not as the specimen: the print body is watertight with no enclosed void, but 18% of the twin surface it derives from is closure where the scanner saw nothing, and its stock and fills are declared. The two-solver comparison is verification on identical cells and does not depend on this. The cell-size rows and the place of the worst corner describe this study body's voxel model, not the specimen; whether the worst corner lies on acquired surface is not established."
 },
